    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43261" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐτησ-ίαι</span></b> , οἱ, gen.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐτησίων</span> Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
			1.425
		</span></i>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔτος</span>):—with or without
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνεμοι</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>periodic winds</i>, esp. those blowing from
			north-west during the summer, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.140
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i><i>Aër.</i><i><span class="en">
				10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				4.31
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				361b35
			</span></i>; of the <i>southerly monsoon</i> in the Indian Ocean,
				<i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>An.</u>
				6.21.1
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Εὖροι ἐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Posidon.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				3.2.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> sg., as
			nickname of Antipater, who reigned for forty-five days, <i>King of
				the Dog-days,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PCair.Zen.
				19.6
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Fr.Hist.</u>
				4.6
			</span></i>.</div>
